@startuml
title Customer Activity Analytics — Quality, security and delivery constraints
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor<<MANDATORY>> #FFB3B3
  BackgroundColor<<MUST_HAVE>> #FFD699
  BackgroundColor<<NICE_TO_HAVE>> #D6EAF8
}

actor "Developer / Reviewer" as Reviewer
actor "Customer Care\nOperator" as Operator

rectangle "Customer Activity Analytics\n<<system boundary>>" as SystemBoundary {
  package "Reproducibility and verification" {
    usecase "Reproduce System Locally\n[NFR-REP-001]" as NF_Reproduce <<MANDATORY>>
    usecase "Verify Baseline Deterministically\n[NFR-VER-001]" as NF_Verify <<MANDATORY>>
    usecase "Complete Baseline Analysis\nwithout External LLM\n[CON-AI-001]" as NF_Offline <<MANDATORY>>
  }

  package "Access and data controls" {
    usecase "Use Protected Capabilities Only\nWhen Authenticated\n[NFR-SEC-001]" as NF_Secure <<MUST_HAVE>>
  }
}

Reviewer -- NF_Reproduce
Reviewer -- NF_Verify
Reviewer -- NF_Offline
Operator -- NF_Secure
Operator -- NF_Offline

note bottom of SystemBoundary
  <<constraint>> System-wide defaults
  Demonstration data is synthetic by default [CON-DATA-001].
  Transmission to an external AI provider is opt-in [CON-AI-002].
end note

note bottom of NF_Verify
  Pass/fail is executable evidence. The SRS specifies what must be verifiable;
  it does not hand-maintain current test status.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Notation |= Meaning |
  | Solid actor association | Direct concern/use interaction |
  | Package | Logical grouping inside the system boundary |
  | <<constraint>> note on boundary | System-wide constraint |
  |= Colour |= Delivery priority |
  |<#FFB3B3> | MANDATORY |
  |<#FFD699> | MUST_HAVE |
  |<#D6EAF8> | NICE_TO_HAVE |
  | NICE_TO_HAVE shown in legend | Valid delivery level even when no use case in this view currently uses it |
endlegend
@enduml
